EmmcpMcpActivityTab=MCP activity
EmmcpMcpActivityIntro=This page records the calls received by the external MCP server: who called which tool, when, and with what outcome. It serves troubleshooting, but also lets you watch how much data is being read — Dolibarr permissions say what a user may see, not how much of it.
EmmcpMcpSettings=Settings
EmmcpMcpLogEnabled=Log MCP calls
EmmcpMcpLogEnabledDesc=On by default. Without a log there is no record of what an agent read.
EmmcpMcpLogArguments=Record call arguments
EmmcpMcpLogArgumentsDesc=Arguments show which data was asked for, which is what makes the log actually usable. They can contain personal data: turn this off if your policy requires it. Results are never recorded either way.
EmmcpMcpRetention=Log retention
EmmcpMcpRetentionDesc=Older rows are deleted when the log is purged. Default: 90 days.
EmmcpMcpRateLimit=Call limit per user
EmmcpMcpRateLimitDesc=Maximum tool calls allowed within the window. 0 disables the limit. Only tool calls count: connecting and listing tools consume nothing.
EmmcpMcpCallsPer=calls per
EmmcpMcpAlertThreshold=Alert threshold
EmmcpMcpAlertThresholdDesc=Emails the administrator when a user reaches this many calls within the window. 0 disables the alert. Set it below the limit to be warned before anyone is blocked.
EmmcpMcpAlertEmail=Alert recipient
EmmcpMcpAlertEmailDesc=Leave empty to use the company email address.
EmmcpMcpAlertCooldown=Delay between alerts
EmmcpMcpAlertCooldownDesc=For the same user. Stops one intensive session from sending dozens of emails. Default: 720 minutes.
EmmcpMcpSettingsSaved=Settings saved
EmmcpMcpAlertEmailInvalid=Invalid email address: the other settings were saved.
